TEXT -416 312 Left 2 ;When firing: Zener-Diode breaks down and lets through approx. 2.7 A limited by a 1.5 Ohm resistor\n \nWhen checking continuity: Zener-Diode blocks off firing path and current is limited to approx. 10 uA by 300k resistor\n \nShottkey Diodes prevent any current from going into the DO's\nInverter causes inverted signals between firing mosfet and continuity mosfet to ensure both have inverted states at all times
TEXT 880 -800 Left 2 ;When firing: Disconnect 3V3 source to simulate open firing MOSFET\n \nWhen checking for continuity: Disconnect 9V source to simulate open continuity MOSFET\nand disconnect firing path to simulate a blocking Zener-Diode
